invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the correction for an even scalar adds -G by the incomplete
  addition. For k = n - 1 the sum before it is the point at infinity,
  which the incomplete addition cannot read, so k * G comes out as the
  point at infinity where -G is right. bin/p256_equiv_test multiplies G
  by n - 1.

--- old
    p256_wide_point_add_affine(&corrected, &sum, &entry);
--- new
    p256_wide_point_add_affine_incomplete(&corrected, &sum, &entry);
